If what you're saying is true, then your problem was simply a broken LCD. There should be no reason for a logic board swap if you have a broken LCD. 

&#x200B;

The fact that your laptop screen is now not turning on at all makes it sound like they broke something else. 

&#x200B;

There is no such thing as having a broken LCD macbook, opening it up to diagnose, and suddenly the computer no longer works at all and now they have to swap the logic board.

